next
  Summary: Combat takeover, fire discipline, sniper hold, friendly fire, NPC ammo, weapon jam, danger rework, survivor-gate kills, healing fixes, AOEngine

  Combat
    - Added an intermittent combat takeover: AlifeTactics borrows a stalker for one committed maneuver.
      Stalkers kite when crowded, retreat to cover or flee when hurt, and hold sniper aim when stalled.
      A borrowed stalker holds fire when it has no clear shot instead of firing into cover.
      Companions are left out of the takeover by default (MCM > Combat > Maneuvers).
    - Added a same-faction friendly-fire damage block (MCM > Effectiveness > Crossfire, default on).
      A stalker that hits a same-faction teammate deals no damage, tunable back up to full vanilla.
    - Removed the standalone Stance Switch system, now folded into the takeover's sniper hold.

  Effectiveness
    - Added a survivor gate to Hit Sharing (MCM, default on).
      A kill that drops the victim outright no longer discloses the shooter, so stealth kills stay quiet.

  Mechanics
    - Added NPC armor-piercing ammo drawn from the boxes they carry, not a magic-refilled fixed type.
      Veteran-rank and higher NPCs fire AP with real ballistics until their carried supply runs out.
      Tunable in configs/alifetactics/at_ammo.ltx (MCM > Mechanics > Ammo, default on).
    - Added NPC weapon jam suppression that stops the demonized per-rank jam-reload loop for NPCs.
      Actor jams stay vanilla (MCM > Mechanics > Jamming, default on, needs demonized 2026.6.1+).

  Danger
    - Added fixes for six Anomaly xr_danger bugs via a full-file override and paired ltx.
      Hits, ricochets, and nearby gunshots each use their own config row instead of one shared row.
      Three danger improvements are MCM-toggleable on the Effectiveness > Danger page.
    - Changed corpse danger to last 15 game minutes (was 12 seconds), with weather-scaled detection range.

  Fixes
    - Fixed limping to match the NPC's weapon, and to stop after HP recovers or during combat.
    - Fixed healing NPCs freezing in place and ignoring enemies that appear mid-gesture.
    - Fixed a crash on a torn-down attacker reference during the attack-sound danger dispatch.

  Compatibility
    - Added AOEngine v0.55+ support.

1.0.0
  Summary: First release, hit sharing, NPC self-healing fix, per-rank accuracy, long-range rifle crouch
  First release. Four independent systems on top of one internal core. Full MCM configuration.
  Added: Hit Sharing - on first faction-enemy hit, force-disclose shooter to every online squadmate (force_set_goodwill, enable_memory_object, register_in_combat). Distant patrols and suppressor victims now engage on hit 1. Disclosure decays after the configured retention (default 2 game minutes of no further hits from that shooter), then re-fires on the next hit. New squad members inherit existing disclosures on spawn. Previously-offline shooters coming back online replay disclosure to every member of the squads tracking them.
  Added: NPC Self-Healing - DLTX overlay restores vanilla medkit and bandage item lists in xr_eat_medkit. Heal rate multiplier, per-rank healing-charge probability (novice, experienced, veteran, master), limping overlay, heal animation.
  Added: Accuracy - per-shot, per-rank NPC dispersion curve replacing the engine's broken rank curve. 8 per-tier dispersion sliders (novice 1.00 to legend 0.38).
  Added: Stance Switch - long-range rifle carriers (DMRs, battle rifles, bolt-actions: SVD, Mosin, SVT40, SKS, M82 and the rest of the kind=w_sniper LTX class) crouch when engine selects LookOut or HoldPosition. Crouch carries forward into KillEnemy, WaitInCover, HoldAmbushLocation through body_state inheritance.
  Added: MCM reset-to-defaults button (Development tab).
  Added: console test commands at_spawn, at_spawn_veteran, at_spawn_master, at_spawn_far, at_dump.
